  "chapter": {
    "number": 54,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(55) For the end, among Hymns of instruction by David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Listen, O God, to my prayer; and disregard not my supplication.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Attend to me, and listen to me: I was grieved in my meditation, and troubled;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "because of the voice of the enemy, and because of the oppression of the sinner: for they brought iniquity against me, and were wrathfully angry with me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My heart was troubled within me; and the fear of death fell upon me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Fear and trembling came upon me, and darkness covered me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And I said, O that I had wings as those of a dove! then would I flee away, and be at rest.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Behold! I have fled afar off, and lodged in the wilderness. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I waited for him that should deliver me from distress of spirit and tempest.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Destroy, O Lord, and divide their tongues: for I have seen iniquity and gain saying in the city.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Day and night",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 99
          },
          {
            "text": "he shall go round about it upon its walls: iniquity and sorrow and unrighteousness are in the midst of it;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and usury and craft have not failed from its streets.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For if an enemy had reproached me, I would have endured it; and if one who hated me had spoken vauntingly against me, I would have hid myself from him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But you, O man like minded, my guide, and my acquaintance,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "who in companionship with me sweetened our food: we walked in the house of God in concord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let death come upon them, and let them go down alive into Hades, for iniquity is in their dwellings, in the midst of them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I cried to God, and the Lord listened to me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Evening, and morning, and at noon I will declare and make known my wants: and he shall hear my voice.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He shall deliver my soul in peace from them that draw near to me: for they were with me in many cases.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "God shall hear, and bring them low, even he that has existed from eternity. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 100
          },
          {
            "text": "For they suffer no reverse, and therefore they have not feared God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He has reached forth his hand for retribution; they have profaned his covenant.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They were scattered at the anger of his countenance, and his heart drew near",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 101
          },
          {
            "text": "them. His words were smoother than oil, yet are they darts.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Cast your care upon the Lord, and he shall",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 102
          },
          {
            "text": "sustain you; he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But you, O God, shall bring them down to the pit of destruction; bloody and crafty men shall not live out half their days; but I will hope in you, O Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 99,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, it, sc. iniquity.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 54,
          "verse": 10
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 100,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, they have nothing to give in exchange, q. d. to redeem their souls. Compare Ps. 48. 7,8. Mark 8:37.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 54,
          "verse": 19
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 101,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Compare Heb. and A. V.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 54,
          "verse": 21
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 102,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, nourish.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 54,
          "verse": 22
        }
      }
    ]
  },
